  "note": "Municipal elections, 15 January 1932. Only seven candidates came forward for the fifteen seats on the enlarged Urban District Council, so there was no poll: the seven were returned unopposed and eight retiring members were declared deemed re-elected, the South Ward pair chosen by lot (Lisburn Standard, 8 January 1932, p. 8). M'Nally and Barbour were nominated; the two vacancies among the four retiring councillors were decided by lot, and Chambers and Frazer were declared deemed re-elected. Returned unopposed."
